# Known pitfalls (read before a “quick fix”)

## Terrain / shadows / cap
- Dual mesh / chunky terrain / synced height texture → breaks shadows and pick. **Do not touch.**
- `receiveShadow` + small shadow frustum = dark blotches / missing shadows.
- Cap clip (`uViewAxis`, `uVisibleDot`): seam = bad view axis or unsynced uniforms across materials.
- `shadowMap.autoUpdate` must stay on while terrain casts/receives shadow.

## Normals and morph
- Full-planet `computeVertexNormals()` after morph = frame spike. Use `recomputeNormalsPartial` only.
- Forgotten `needsUpdate` on position/color = “morph invisible”.
- Wet/ocean flood outside the dirty region = stutter on every hill.

## Memory / FX
- PointLight per flame without `MAX_FIRE_LIGHTS` → GPU death.
- Dispose without `parent.remove` → ghost objects in the scene.
- FOW ghost: `clone(true)` only lazy (`ensureWatcherGhost` / trees), not every frame.

## Game logic
- Damage loops must skip `remote` / `godMode` / `immortal` / `dead` consistently with other spells.
- `wetness` ≠ height below waterline (dry pit vs ocean).
- Wizard in water: `wizardMinLand`, drown, `wizardWaterSpeedMul` — do not change one without checking the others.

## Net
- Remote movement via `walk` intent = desync; `pose` is authoritative.
- Double-handling cast (local + echo) without owner checks = double damage/FX.

## LLM regression habits
- “Optimization” that changes spell VFX appearance.
- Adding quality presets / a second resolution path.
- 500+ line “cleanup” refactor during a one-line bugfix.
